Use your image generation tool to make ONE image, 1024 x 1536 (portrait), a finished game UI design sheet for a Roblox game called Arrow Legends.

What it is: the "NEW ENEMY!" screen that pops up over the game the first time the player meets a new kind of enemy. It must look like it belongs to the same set as the FIRST reference image (the game's VICTORY screen): exactly the same blocky pixel-art UI language - chunky stair-stepped panel edges with stepped corners, flat 2-3 tone shading, thick near-black (#1B1B2B) ink outlines, a big ribbon banner across the top with folded tails, bold chunky white pixel lettering with dark outline, small square rivets, floating voxel cubes as decoration, a dark backdrop around the panel. Same proportions and polish as that screen. No smooth gradients, no blur.

Layout, top to bottom:
1. A big ribbon banner across the top with folded tails, reading exactly "NEW ENEMY!" in big chunky white pixel letters with a dark outline. The banner is themed to the AREA (see below) - its colours, its material and the little decorations growing on or hanging from it come from that area.
2. Under it a small plaque reading exactly the AREA NAME given below, in small pixel capitals.
3. A big picture window in the middle of the panel showing the ENEMY (see below) as a 2D blocky pixel-art picture, drawn faithfully from its reference image (same shape, colours, face and details), seen from the front three-quarter view, big and centred, on a scenic backdrop of the area (simple, flat, pixel style) with light rays behind it.
4. A name plate under the picture reading exactly the ENEMY NAME given below, in big chunky pixel capitals.
5. A description box under the name, with exactly the DESCRIPTION text given below in small clean white pixel letters, on two or three lines.
6. At the bottom a big chunky button reading exactly "GOT IT!".

Spell every word exactly as given. No other text anywhere. The whole panel's colours (frame, boxes, button) follow the area theme, not the blue of the reference.


AREA: "WINDSWEPT CLIFFS" - grey-blue slate cliff tops floating in a sea of white cloud, short bright grass on the rims, glowing pale-blue wind streaks across the stone, rope and plank bridges, strings of bright prayer flags (red, yellow, green, blue) on stone posts. The banner is slate stone and weathered wood, with prayer flags and little tufts of grass on and hanging from it, white wind swirls curling round its tails; the frame is grey-blue slate with grass and small prayer flags. Second reference image: the Windswept Cliffs area.
ENEMY: the Harpy - third reference image (its model sheet): a navy-indigo voxel owl-bird with a lavender chest, a bone-white owl-skull mask with a short hooked beak and glowing pale-blue eyes, a spiky purple-magenta crest, huge spread wings fading indigo to purple to magenta-pink, short brown legs. Draw it faithfully, in the blocky style, hovering.
ENEMY NAME: "HARPY"
DESCRIPTION: "Flies over walls and dives where it marks the ground. Step out of the ring!"

Save the image in the current directory as sheet_windswept_cliffs_a.png
